Privacy Policy — Snapp: MediaCleaner
Last updated: February 2026
Snapp — MediaCleaner (“the App”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use the App.
1. Information We Collect
Snapp does not collect, store, or share any personal information.
The App does not require registration and does not collect data such as:
Name, email address, or phone number
Location data
Contacts
Advertising identifiers
Browsing or tracking information
2. Photo Library Access
Snapp requires access to your device’s Photo Library to provide its core functionality, including:
Displaying photos and videos for sorting
Allowing you to mark items for deletion
Deleting selected media only with your confirmation
Organizing media into albums
All photo and video processing happens locally on your device. Snapp does not upload your media to any servers.
3. Local Data Storage
The App stores limited technical information only on your device to function properly, such as:
Items you have already reviewed
Items marked for deletion
Basic statistics (for example, freed storage size)
Subscription and trial status
This information is stored locally and is never shared externally.
4. Subscriptions and Payments
Snapp offers optional Premium features through Apple In-App Purchases.
All payments are processed securely by Apple. Snapp does not collect or store any payment or credit card information.
5. Third-Party Services
Snapp does not use third-party analytics, advertising SDKs, or tracking technologies.
6. Data Sharing
We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties.
7. Children’s Privacy
The App is not intended for children under the age of 13 and does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
8. Managing Permissions
You can manage or revoke photo access permissions at any time in:
Settings → Privacy & Security → Photos → Snapp
9. Contact
If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us:
